> Don't bring them into sokoban.

Bad advice.

Sokoban gets _easier_ as you go up, unless
you gain levels along the way. Having your
pets do the fighting for you along the way
saves you from having to gain XP.

Better advice: have some plan for controlling
your pets in Sokoban. Any of these will work:

1) carry a stack of cursed darts or arrows or
daggers, to drop to prevent your pets from
getting ahead of your pushed boulders.

2) Keep your pets on leash.

3) Keep your pets on the level just below
the one where you're pushing boulders, until
monsters arrive that require your pets'
attention, shuffle pets up and down often.

4) Acquire and use a magic whistle to pull
pets away from overpowerful monsters, out
of the way of your boulder pushing.

As for pets attacking overpowerful monsters,
a good way to handle that is to assure that
two or more pets a) split the monster's
attacks, while b) attacking the monster
together. Leashes, magic whistles, or just
herding pets by interposing the PC where you
don't want the pets to go, can assomplish
this.

